{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/875849-some-new-shifter-gifts-and-a-new-rite","id":875849,"title":"Some new shifter gifts and a new rite","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-27T12:26:24-07:00","id":875849,"title":"Some new shifter gifts and a new rite","content":"OK, so i am not having to hunt for an old thread or two where this has been done before, here are some gifts and a new ritual i have made up over the many years i played werewolf..<br /> <br /> First up is my new rite... Rite of the Kin seeking. Level 4. Most often used by Were-bears, but can be used by any who learn the ritual.<br /> <br /> A Gurahl can, only use this potent rite, once a month (lunar cycle). When the Gurahl uses it, he gets a feeling for those shifters who are pre-change and/or those who have just undergone their first change. It allows the Gurahl in question, or allies of his, to track down these lost cubs before 3rd parties find them. If the 'soon-to-be' shifter HAS a kin fetch spirit (via the rite), it does NOT show them. For those 'pre first change' it only tells of those who are NEAR (within 2 lunar cycles) of the change. Note, that if the rite performer has no knowledge of say Annassi, he can't use this ritual to locate them. Also to find those of other fera types, one of those types must be present during the ritual being performed to stand a chance of locating them.<br /> <br /> System: The cost for activating this rite, is 5 gnosis which can come solely from the Gurahl (or other Fera) performing the ritual, OR contributed to by all present if multiple shifters are there. It requires 4 uninterrupted hours of preparation and 'pomp'. The Gurahl also must have at least 1 other Fera present. The performer of the ritual make 2 separate rolls, the first one is INT + Rites at diff 7 (6 if he has more than the 1 required Fera present. If he has 3 or more different Fera types present, the diff drops to 5).<br /> First roll:<br /> 1 success - 1 mile radius<br /> 2 successes - 5 miles<br /> 3 successes - 10 miles<br /> 4 successes - 20 miles<br /> 5 successes - 50 miles<br /> 6+ successes - 100 miles<br /> <br /> The second roll is PER + Enigmas, diff 8 (7 if has 1 other Fera besides the required one, 6 if he has 3 or more Fera types present), and the number of successes determines how well he reads the seeking.<br /> Second roll:<br /> 1 success - 1 'ping' for a shifter who meets the criteria, but no direction or whether they are near the first change or have just had it.<br /> 2 successes - As 1, but does give direction and a rough estimate of distance.<br /> 3 successes - Gurahl can pick either near first change or post first change, and knows how many of that type are in the range, and the 'localization' is to within 1 mile.<br /> 4 successes - gets both for type, and localization is to within 1/3rd of a mile.<br /> 5 successes - knows how long the pre-changed has to go, or how long it has been since the first change, and localization is to within 1 city block (average of 100mX100m)<br /> 6+ successes - localization is to the specific building.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <u>New Gifts</u><br /> Silver slip, Rank 3 gift.<br /> This gift is taught mostly to Gurahl, but is also known to some Children of Gaia and can be learned by anyone who willingly has gone to Erebus, the lake of silver, since it is only taught by the lady of the lake herself. Using the gift, it ties the shifter who activates it to the lake, so any time he goes into the Umbra (Or for Gurahl, rends the gauntlet opens a portal TO the lake) with someone, it automatically takes them TO Erebus.<br /> System: The character spends a point of Gnosis, and for the remainder of the scene, they are directly tied to the umbral real of Erebus, so if the Garou/Gurahl (or other fera) are wishing to, they can Drag/throw creatures of the wyrm To erebus to get cleansed. It can only be used once every OTHER lunar cycle, as too frequent use will anger the lady of the lake, and will cause the user to be required to spend a full month bathing there.<br /> <br /> Luna's Fertility, Rank 6 gift.<br /> This little known and very potent gift is only taught by Luna herself to those few Fera who achieve legendary status. It can be used in one of two ways. The first way is to increase the gift owner's fertility, which increases his or her chance to produce fellow true blood offspring to 20% during a 3 month period. It can only be used Once in his or her lifetime.<br /> The second method is that it can restore someone's lost fertility via battle wounds or disfigurement, even to Metis, though that is very frowned on. <br /> System: there is a cost of 1 Permanent Gnosis for using it in the first manner, or to heal someone of their infertility, it requires 2 Gnosis to be spent. If used in the latter method to restore someone's infertility, it can be used only once a calendar year. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}